,"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YYF233333/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T11:16:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T11:16:05Z","body":"> But performance should be tested first. This struct is used a lot, and changing alignment and using bitfields can have performance impact. It's not worth saving memory if it decreases performance in any way.\r\n\r\nAgree, but layout related performance issues are hard to measure. My initial consideration is that 32B may make some difference because we can put two `PropertyInfo` in one cacheline. I'll try to find some useful benchmarks.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713743245/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]